ingest accepts a slice that ends inside an atomic batch: part of the batch
is published, and a rotation after the slice seals its BulkBegin into a file
with no BulkEnd, so a reopen drops entries the follower synced (#188).
Guarded-by: "ingest refuses a slice that ends inside an atomic batch"

diff --git a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
index 3838253..8b00e8f 100644
--- a/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
+++ b/bytecaskdb/bytecask.cppm
@@ -6658,7 +6658,7 @@ void DB::ingest(std::span<const DataEntryView> entries) {
   // A slice published as given would expose half a batch, and a rotation
   // after it would seal the BulkBegin into a file with no BulkEnd: recovery
   // then drops entries this follower acknowledged and synced (#188).
-  if (in_batch) {
+  if (false && in_batch) {
     throw std::invalid_argument{
         "ingest: the slice ends inside an atomic batch; cut slices after a "
         "BulkEnd or a standalone entry"};
